## 🎤 Interview Talking Points

| Question | Answer |
|---|---|
| **"Why hybrid over pure dense?"** | Dense misses keyword/exact-match queries. BM25 catches them. RRF fuses both — measured +22% NDCG@5. |
| **"Why a reranker if embeddings are good?"** | Bi-encoders score query/doc separately (fast but coarse). Cross-encoders see them together (slow but accurate). I use bi-encoder for top-20 retrieval, cross-encoder for top-5 reranking. |
| **"Why no Elasticsearch for BM25?"** | For <1M chunks, `rank_bm25` is sufficient and avoids extra infrastructure. For scale I'd migrate to Elasticsearch or OpenSearch. |
| **"How do you reduce hallucinations?"** | 4 layers: constrained prompting, verifier agent with NLI entailment check, retry loop, and citation requirement. |
| **"Why ChromaDB?"** | Free, persistent, supports metadata filtering, sufficient for <1M vectors. For scale I'd swap to Pinecone or Weaviate — same retriever interface. |
| **"How do you evaluate RAG?"** | RAGAS (faithfulness, relevance, precision, recall) + custom citation accuracy + 100-query golden dataset across 4 difficulty tiers + CI/CD gate on regression. |
| **"Cost optimization tricks?"** | Model routing (mini for cheap tasks), semantic caching, prompt compression with LLMLingua, embedding cache, hard token budget. |
| **"Why Streamlit not React?"** | Streamlit ships fast for ML demos with native Python streaming and component model. Recruiters care about the AI engineering, not frontend stack. |

